  <!-- Criteria component attribute values -->
  <xs:simpleType name="criteriaComponentType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">Kind of input of a criterion. All values are implemented by both engines except picklist (React only) and the deprecated progress (not implemented as a criterion by any engine; it only exists as a grid column).</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="hidden" />
      <xs:enumeration value="text" />
      <xs:enumeration value="numeric" />
      <xs:enumeration value="select" />
      <xs:enumeration value="suggest" />
      <xs:enumeration value="suggest-multiple" />
      <xs:enumeration value="select-multiple" />
      <xs:enumeration value="picklist" />
      <xs:enumeration value="date" />
      <xs:enumeration value="date-range">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">A pair of dates (start and end of a period) in one criterion. The end cannot be
            before the start, and quick presets can be configured with the presets attribute. The criterion sends two
            parameters, "id.from" and "id.to" (null when empty), both as dd/mm/yyyy dates. The default value is a list of two
            dates separated by a comma ("01/01/2026,31/01/2026").</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="time" />
      <xs:enumeration value="filtered-calendar" />
      <xs:enumeration value="color" />
      <xs:enumeration value="progress">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">Deprecated in AWE 5.0 and removed in 6.0: no client engine implements it as a criterion. The progress grid column stays.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="textarea" />
      <xs:enumeration value="uploader" />
      <xs:enumeration value="checkbox" />
      <xs:enumeration value="radio" />
      <xs:enumeration value="button-checkbox" />
      <xs:enumeration value="button-radio" />
      <xs:enumeration value="password" />
      <xs:enumeration value="text-view" />
      <xs:enumeration value="markdown-editor" />
    </xs:restriction>
  </xs:simpleType>

  <!-- Column component attribute values -->
  <xs:simpleType name="columnComponentType">
    <xs:annotation>
      <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">Component of a grid column. Most values reuse the criteria of the same name for editing; radio and button-radio columns show the options of their list in every cell, like a select column. link is React only; formatted-text renders sanitized HTML.</xs:documentation>
    </xs:annotation>
    <xs:restriction base="xs:string">
      <xs:enumeration value="text" />
      <xs:enumeration value="numeric" />
      <xs:enumeration value="select" />
      <xs:enumeration value="suggest" />
      <xs:enumeration value="suggest-multiple" />
      <xs:enumeration value="select-multiple" />
      <xs:enumeration value="date" />
      <xs:enumeration value="time" />
      <xs:enumeration value="filtered-calendar" />
      <xs:enumeration value="color" />
      <xs:enumeration value="progress">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">Progress bar of a numeric value, from 0 to 100 by default. The React engine tunes it with bar-min and bar-max (the scale, with a zero mark and negative fill below 0), bar-second-field (a thinner second bar, such as a target), bar-stack-fields (stacked segments) and bar-leaf-only (tree grids); AngularJS ignores these options. Print and export write the cell value.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="textarea" />
      <xs:enumeration value="uploader" />
      <xs:enumeration value="checkbox" />
      <xs:enumeration value="radio">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">Single choice among the options of a list, shown in every cell as a row of radio buttons with their labels. The options come from the list of the column exactly as for a select column (initial-load and target-action, a query or an enumerated with value and label), and the value of the chosen option is the value of the cell: it is sent like the one of a select column, as one value per row. The column is sortable and can be validated (a required column needs a choice in every row). Left and right arrow keys move the choice between the options of the cell. A read-only column cannot be changed.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="button-radio">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">Same choice as the radio column, drawn as one joined bar of toggle buttons (a segmented control), like the button-radio criterion: adjacent buttons share their borders and only the ends of the bar are rounded. The options come from the list of the column, as for a select column, and the value of the chosen option is the value of the cell.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="image" />
      <xs:enumeration value="icon" />
      <xs:enumeration value="sparkline">
        <xs:annotation>
          <xs:documentation xml:lang="en">Small chart of a series of numbers, drawn inside the cell. The value of the cell is a JSON array of numbers, for example [3, 5, -1, 8], either as text or as an already parsed list; any other value (empty, not a list, or a list with something that is not a number) leaves the cell empty. The drawing is chosen with sparkline-type, and sparkline-color, sparkline-negative-color, sparkline-last-point and sparkline-min-max adjust it. Hovering a point shows its value in a tooltip. Both client engines draw the same SVG, which is 100 by 24 pixels. The cell is not editable.</xs:documentation>
        </xs:annotation>
      </xs:enumeration>
      <xs:enumeration value="password" />
      <xs:enumeration value="text-view" />
      <xs:enumeration value="button" />
